# README sync

`README.md` is the user-facing doc. Update it in the **same change** when you alter behavior users see or operators configure.

## Update README when you change

- Scoring or tie-breaker rules
- Poller interval, announcement behavior, or which leagues are polled
- Setup: env vars (`.env.example`) and other league-bot configuration
- Configuration behavior that is not obvious from `/help` alone

Link [Discord's bot docs](https://docs.discord.com/developers/bots/overview) for creating an application and inviting the bot. Slash command names, options, and permissions live in command docstrings and `/help`; update those in `src/commands/`.

## Skip README for

- Internal refactors with no user-visible change
- DB schema, API client, or test-only changes (unless they change commands or scoring)

## What to update

| Change | README section |
|--------|----------------|
| New command | Command docstring in `src/commands/` (shown by `/help`) |
| Config / league season behavior | **Setup** |
| Points or tie-breakers | **Leagues** table |
| Env vars | **Environment variables** table + `.env.example` |
| Dev workflow | **Local development** |

Keep `AGENTS.md` for architecture and agent conventions only — not duplicate user docs there.
